<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Frederick I, Elector of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1503–1554</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as John Frederick the Magnanimous</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Frederick I, called the Magnanimous, was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> from 1532 to 1547 and a leader of the Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-league">Schmalkaldic League</a>. Defeated and captured by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhlberg">Battle of Mühlberg</a> in 1547, he lost the electoral title and much of his land to his cousin Maurice of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albertine-line">Albertine line</a>. Released in 1552, he had planned the school at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>, opened in 1548, that became its university.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-frederick-i-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="John Frederick I, Elector of Saxony" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_Cranach_d._%C3%84._044FXD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
